cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite both the paper and the dataset using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "AAPF Validation Dataset: Cross-Page-Size ESE Format Changes in Windows Server 2025"
abstract: >-
  Companion artifacts for the paper "Silent Evidence Loss in Windows Server 2025:
  Cross-Page-Size ESE Format Changes and Their Forensic Integrity Implications"
  (Forensic Science International: Digital Investigation, 2026). Includes:
  (a) source-level patches for libesedb that resolve a previously unreported
  family of WS2025 itagState reinterpretation failures spanning 4 KiB, 16 KiB,
  and 32 KiB pages with a single one-line universal patch;
  (b) a Rust-based NTDS.dit analysis tool (Poneglyph) incorporating the universal
  patch;
  (c) 14 ESE database samples (ntds.dit, DataStore.edb, WebCacheV01.dat,
  SRUDB.dat) captured under the Automated Artifact Population Framework on
  Windows Server 2019 and Windows Server 2025 across Clean, Crashed, and
  Locked snapshot states;
  (d) reproduction scripts and expected outputs.
